  "claim": "An airport is connected to Marquette from the east by the road that is adjacent to Marquette Mountain's base area's parking lot. Both this airport and Brainerd Lakes Regional Airport are not located in Europe.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Sawyer International Airport. Sentence: Sawyer International Airport (IATA: MQT, ICAO: KSAW, FAA LID: SAW) is a county owned public use airport in Marquette County, Michigan, United States.\nPage: Brainerd Lakes Regional Airport. Sentence: Brainerd Lakes Regional Airport (IATA: BRD, ICAO: KBRD, FAA LID: BRD) is a public use airport located three nautical miles (6 km) northeast of the central business district of Brainerd, a city in Crow Wing County, Minnesota, United States.\nPage: M-553 (Michigan highway). Sentence: M-553 connects Marquette with Sawyer International Airport at the unincorporated community of K.I. Sawyer AFB, the former site of a US Air Force base, in the Sands Plains area of Marquette County.\nPage: Marquette Mountain. Sentence: The base area's parking lot is adjacent to highway M-553.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Sawyer International Airport. Sentence: Sawyer International Airport (IATA: MQT, ICAO: KSAW, FAA LID: SAW) is a county owned public use airport in Marquette County, Michigan, United States.\nPage: Brainerd Lakes Regional Airport. Sentence: Brainerd Lakes Regional Airport (IATA: BRD, ICAO: KBRD, FAA LID: BRD) is a public use airport located three nautical miles (6 km) northeast of the central business district of Brainerd, a city in Crow Wing County, Minnesota, United States.\nPage: M-553 (Michigan highway). Sentence: M-553 connects Marquette with Sawyer International Airport at the unincorporated community of K.I. Sawyer AFB, the former site of a US Air Force base, in the Sands Plains area of Marquette County.\nPage: Marquette Mountain. Sentence: The base area's parking lot is adjacent to highway M-553.",
